{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/721668-solar-xp","id":721668,"title":"Solar XP","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Solar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-10-23T20:56:01-07:00","id":721668,"title":"Solar XP","content":"Having run and played games for many years, I don't really like giving out XP for roleplaying (it makes the players who don't get it annoyed, and requires me to constantly be thinking about whether the players should be getting it for whatever they're doing, rather than enjoying the game).<br /> I also don't like, generally, giving players different amounts of XP (there are some exceptions: I'm willing to give out extra XP to support characters whose powers are all about buffing other players rather than being awesome at combat or socialising themselves, as it benefits the whole party, and I don't mind people with suboptimal builds getting more XP). A small amount doesn't matter, but I've played games where, say, two or three Qin characters had 70xp and two or three had 150, or even worse a Vamp Larp where new characters had 0xp and old characters had hundreds, and what tends to happen is the low XP characters die over and over again.<br /> <br /> So, I'm a bit wary of Solar XP. But on the other hand, from the way Holden was talking, it sounds like the balance of the game expects you to give out Solar XP: he mentioned that one of the important things with Martial Arts is that you get XP to spend on it as well as your Solar charms, hence the high cost of it (merit, buying each ability separately).<br /> This makes me think that not giving out Solar XP would be problematic, and make Martial Artists (and sorcerers I suppose) perhaps weaker compared to characters who are focused on normal charms.<br /> <br /> So, my first thought of a solution is to give out 5 or 10 Solar XP at the end of each story as a story reward, and just give out 5 regular XP per session.<br /> <br /> But would that be enough? Due to its nature, I can't really tell how much Solar XP it's expected the characters will earn. Maybe about 2 a session, -ish?<br /> (Also, I don't imagine this is an issue that would become apparent one way or the other for about a year or so, at which point it might be awkward to change)<br /> <br /> This also applies to making high XP characters.<br /> The game I play will hopefully convert to 3rd ed (the ST said he wanted to read the book before deciding, and I doubt he's had time yet), and we have more than 700xp. Obviously with free essence and excellencies that translates into less 3rd ed XP, but we'd still be effectively 500xp characters, or something like that.<br /> If he wants to give us the same amount of XP as he did before, would us having, say, 500 regular XP (rather than 400 regular XP and 100 Solar XP or something) be unbalanced?<br /> On the other hand, if he wants to keep us at our current Essence of 4 (there's an argument that converting characters should have 1 less essence, as Essence 1 is the new Essence 2, but they probably shouldn't have more Essence), would giving us 200xp and 300 gold XP work or be horribly unbalanced?<br /> <br /> What do you all think? Obviously I'm most interested in the thoughts of the developers, but I'm interested in anyone's opinion.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:04:13-07:00","id":721701,"title":"","content":"It's actually pretty explicit on page 177 that you can get up to 4 (2 for &quot;expression&quot; and 2 for &quot;role&quot;) Solar XP per session. Having a Flaw that comes up might up that to 6, but I think that's about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm a Woman, I'm a GM. <i>Of course</i> I'm Evil.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/424-dawaterrat","name":"DaWaterRat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar424_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:07:01-07:00","id":721706,"title":"","content":"Solar XP is basically free. If you take two minutes to talk about one of your major or defining intimacies, you get 2. If you ask one of the other players to do something in line with their Caste role, you get 2. Basically, the only way you'll miss out on solar XP is if the circle is split up and people can't get in contact with each other and even then, you'll still get the Expression bonus. <br /> <br /> 5 to 10 solar XP per story is really not enough when it's supposed to be just a little under 50% of the total XP you earn. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:10:18-07:00","id":721713,"title":"","content":"As the occasional ST, I often look for ways to expedite various mechanical concepts. For me, my quick and dirty &quot;fix&quot; for Solar XP would instead offer a free charm or spell of a PCs choice every other session, and a Dot of their choice every third session.<br /> <br /> This solution is probably not for everyone, but I'm throwing it out there for consideration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2034-jaytee","name":"JayTee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2034_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1805"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:23:45-07:00","id":721730,"title":"","content":"I assume by free charm you mean Martial Arts charm.<br /> <br /> Tiresias, you really thin\u200bk it's supposed to be that much, so you're getting 9xp a session? Those seem like liberal interpretations of the way you get them, but I'm not sure.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:24:35-07:00","id":721732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DaWaterRat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/721668-solar-xp?p=721701#post721701\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's actually pretty explicit on page 177 that you can get up to 4 (2 for &quot;expression&quot; and 2 for &quot;role&quot;) Solar XP per session. Having a Flaw that comes up might up that to 6, but I think that's about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope being significantly endangered, hampered, or harmed by a flaw is just one of the 3 options that will allow you to get your expression solar xp for the session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:24:49-07:00","id":721733,"title":"","content":"From the moment the concept was released, I house-ruled that Solar XP is earned by individuals for the table. But I've almost always give people 75% of XP if they miss a session. e.g. person that joins mid-story starts with 75%XP of highest XP player","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2817,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2817-phantom-queen","user":"Phantom Queen","date":". 10-24-2015, 12:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2817-phantom-queen","name":"Phantom Queen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2817_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:32:26-07:00","id":721740,"title":"","content":"I used to give new characters the lowest XP of current players, and not give out XP for missed sessions, but as I said, I saw the problems you got when some players got way ahead of others in terms of XP (especially combat characters).<br /> Earning it for the table probably works if you divide it, but I assume that's what you meant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 10-24-2015, 12:50 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:53:22-07:00","id":721795,"title":"","content":"Another thing I wondered about Solar XP:<br /> <br /> As I understand it, the point of it is that without it people would just spend all their XP on Solar charms because Solar charms are so awesome (I don't see the logic there, there are simpler ways to solve it, but let's go with that).<br /> <br /> Now, Lunar and Sidereal charms are weaker, but maybe not enough that it matters.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dragonblood charms are much weaker, to the extent that you might want to spend all your XP on spells (Terrestrial spells being no weaker when cast by a DB than by a Solar).<br /> So, I wonder if Dragonbloods will either a)not get an equivalent, or b)have Dragonblood XP that you can only spend on charms, so that they buy charms rather than just spells and more stats.\u200b<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T21:59:41-07:00","id":721804,"title":"","content":"I would start by giving out Solar xp liberally. At end if every session, ask the players to justify why they should get the xp. Accept any reasonable justification. Accept any funny or smart one. Accept anything that the player did that made playing the game more fun for everyone. Most players should get all the bonus xp each session. This incentivizes player involvement and reflection on the game. It's also a great way for players to boast and let off steam. He'll, share on last beer at the table and give xp for talking about the awesome session you just had. <br /> <br /> But let the players know that this is a trial run. You might find that the power level increases too quick for you. That's fine. If you think that us happening then let them know, talk to them and hear their thoughts, and then stop the award for a while to let the campaign catch up to the Pcs. You can always go back to giving it out again if you choose. <br /> <br /> You could also slow down the award to half the max value. I don't recommend slowing to a variable amount because the competition can become an issue. Instead, expect to give out all, half, or none of the xp to players that provide a justification for it. <br /> <br /> Also, if someone is struggling to come up a cool thing to justify the xp award, let the other players step up and suggest it. Make it a team effort to show that everyone was in it together.<br /> <br /> Giving out solar xp is also a good way to deal with age old question if what xp to give to folk who miss the game. Give then the regular basic award and the lose out on the solar xp.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:times new roman\">In Honor of <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2746-tgueiros\" target=\"_blank\">TGUEIROS<br /> <br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://www.myidentitydoctor.com/image/cache/data/Website-Product-Photos/medical-awareness/Awareness-Tags/R1C/R1BR-A-Colon-Cancer-Awareness-Ribbon-Charm-216x153.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> N</a>ever Repeat the Dumbness</b></span>","edited":{"userid":1338,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","user":"BvBPL","date":". 10-24-2015, 01:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1338-bvbpl","name":"BvBPL","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T22:05:44-07:00","id":721811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nalak42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/721668-solar-xp?p=721732#post721732\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope being significantly endangered, hampered, or harmed by a flaw is just one of the 3 options that will allow you to get your expression solar xp for the session.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure that the line you quoted was meant to imply that if you did all three options, you could get up to 6 SXP.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T22:15:34-07:00","id":721840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dex Davican</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/721668-solar-xp?p=721811#post721811\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure that the line you quoted was meant to imply that if you did all three options, you could get up to 6 SXP.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope paragraph before it says you have two chances to get solar xp per session for a total of 4. It says you can get one expression and one role and the beginning of expression says you can get two solar xp by completing one of those options per session.<br /> <br /> In short there are three different ways to qualify for your expression points ,assuming you took a flaw, and well role depends on the other castes available in your circle. You can't trigger one of those categories more than once in a session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-23T22:18:38-07:00","id":721845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/721668-solar-xp?p=721795#post721795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I wondered about Solar XP:<br /> <br /> As I understand it, the point of it is that without it people would just spend all their XP on Solar charms because Solar charms are so awesome (I don't see the logic there, there are simpler ways to solve it, but let's go with that).<br /> <br /> Now, Lunar and Sidereal charms are weaker, but maybe not enough that it matters.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dragonblood charms are much weaker, to the extent that you might want to spend all your XP on spells (Terrestrial spells being no weaker when cast by a DB than by a Solar).<br /> So, I wonder if Dragonbloods will either a)not get an equivalent, or b)have Dragonblood XP that you can only spend on charms, so that they buy charms rather than just spells and more stats.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>I would caution against this sort of speculation for a very simple reason. If you're designing the Dragonblooded Charm set and all the other uniquely Dragonblooded rules that you set out to make that will use the 3e core. Starting off with the idea that players will be disincentivized to purchased Dragonblooded charms and find Terrestrial spells more effective and tantalizing is a very very bad place to start. I would expect a thought process to start with examining the play experience of Dragonblooded before and what areas if any that players of Dragonblooded felt a little spread thing when it came to what to prioritize their xp on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"","name":"Guest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/default_avatar_large.png","title":"","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T01:41:06-07:00","id":722280,"title":"","content":"Personally I would make it more or less a group reward so to speak, perhaps give a little extra to someone that's playing something they haven't played before and does really good role playing as a kind of incentive to have them keep on trying new things so to speak.<br /> <br /> What I mean is for example: Myself, I usually play the combat monster, the giant armored beast so to speak and I've played all but one campaign as male characters. So when I suddenly Decided &quot;hey, I wanna try out to play a social female lunar&quot;. that was a completely new territory and it led to some really awesome role play (possibly one of the best sessions I've ever had) that could never have happened with any of my other characters.<br /> I hope I make sense","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I'm making the Tales of Exalts webcomic<br /> <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/50854781/tales-of-exalts\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...ales-of-exalts</a><br /> alchemical report <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/54812164/Alchemical-Report\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/galler...hemical-Report</a><br /> the fall <a href=\"http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall\" target=\"_blank\">http://xanroth.deviantart.com/gallery/55265686/the-fall</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4455-xanroth","name":"Xanroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4455_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1072"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T04:37:03-07:00","id":722565,"title":"","content":"I imagine all my players will get four solar XP basically every session, it's really not difficult to do. The role bonus especially, I mean if you do anything that your caste aligns with at all, bam, there you go. I mean he'll if a dawn has an intimacy towards his circle then any combat involving them triggers it.<br /> <br /> I'd also imagine the other exalt types don't get solar XP. Solars always has a distinct mechanic for rapid growth and terrifying ability to acquire fast power. I predict that Lunars, Sidereals and especially DBs won't have access to that kind of thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T04:41:07-07:00","id":722570,"title":"","content":"I like solar XP. I'd probably add more ways to get all four points per session just to make sure they get handed out. Not that it's hard to get it in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2367-resplendent-fire","name":"Resplendent Fire","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2367_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1887"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-10-24T04:58:55-07:00","id":722593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/solar-exalted/721668-solar-xp?p=721795#post721795\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another thing I wondered about Solar XP:<br /> <br /> As I understand it, the point of it is that without it people would just spend all their XP on Solar charms because Solar charms are so awesome (I don't see the logic there, there are simpler ways to solve it, but let's go with that).<br /> <br /> Now, Lunar and Sidereal charms are weaker, but maybe not enough that it matters.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, Dragonblood charms are much weaker, to the extent that you might want to spend all your XP on spells (Terrestrial spells being no weaker when cast by a DB than by a Solar).<br /> So, I wonder if Dragonbloods will either a)not get an equivalent, or b)have Dragonblood XP that you can only spend on charms, so that they buy charms rather than just spells and more stats.\u200b</div> </div> </div> </div>If Dragon-Blooded get their own Chosen XP (and to the best of my knowledge, I believe they will), I'd expect it to be pretty much identical to Solar XP in function. Dragon-Blooded Charms may be weaker than Solar Charms, but that doesn't mean they are the delicious awesomeness you want to be throwing your xp just as much as a Solar would. Also it would be such a pain in the tuckus if Chosen XP worked differently for just one splat.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}